ProjectCenter document icons
============================

SVG files are the editable sources. The application packages the 48 x 48 RGBA
TIFF versions for compatibility with GNUstep image loading. Normal builds do
not require an SVG renderer. To regenerate TIFFs, run:

    /usr/bin/python3 Images/Documents/render-icons.py

The renderer requires PyGObject, librsvg, and Pillow.

Resources/Info-gnustep.plist maps extensions to icons. PCEditor uses that same
mapping, preserving case so .c receives C and .C receives C++. C++ aliases .cc,
.CC, .cp, .cpp, and .c++ share the C++ icon. Objective-C, Objective-C++, headers,
property lists, syntax definitions, text files, and projects have their own
icons. Other files opened in the text editor, including extensionless files,
use DocumentText. Binary resources handled by other applications retain those
applications' file associations.

Edited variants add an amber dot for unsaved changes.

These icons and their sources are distributed under ProjectCenter's GPL terms;
see COPYING in the repository root.
